How the repository is built and how to add a lab: [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).

## Labs

| lab | topic | report |
|---|---|---|

## Setup

```bash
make setup                          # uv sync + git hooks
make lab N=001 TOPIC=monte-carlo    # scaffold labs/001-monte-carlo from the template
```

## Running a lab

```bash
uv run labs/001-monte-carlo/scripts/run.py           # writes data/ and report/generated/
uv run labs/001-monte-carlo/scripts/run.py seed=1    # Hydra overrides
make report LAB=001                                  # report/report.pdf, built in Docker (TeX Live)
```

Each lab's settings are listed, with defaults and comments, in `labs/<lab>/config/main.yaml`.
